Other Challenges
Quality of Service
Network instability in emerging regions translates into intermittent audio clipping and latency spikes, with 22 % of surveyed enterprises citing occasional service degradation. Mitigating these issues requires adaptive codecs, edge caching and robust QoS policies.
Market Restraints
Legacy Integration Barriers
Many organizations operate mixed technology telephony environments. Aligning SIP appliances with entrenched analog or ISDN switches demands custom gateway development, inflating deployment budgets by 15 25 %. Small  and medium size firms feel the financial pressure most acutely, slowing overall market momentum.
